# Tubidy

> Tubidy is a free music and video search site where you can find songs, artists and music videos and save them as MP3 audio or MP4 video on any phone, right in your browser, without an account.

Tubidy (https://audio.tubidy.com/) is used mostly in South Africa and other countries in southern and eastern Africa. The site is available in English, Spanish, French, Indonesian, Portuguese and Turkish.

## Official site and app
- Tubidy's official website is tubidy.com, which opens at https://audio.tubidy.com/; the older addresses www.tubidy.com and ww3.tubidy.com lead there too.
- The only official app is Tubidy for Android on Google Play (package com.mobiventura.tubidy_music): https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.mobiventura.tubidy_music. Tubidy never distributes APK files.
- Sites and apps that use the Tubidy name at other addresses are not run by Tubidy. Details: https://audio.tubidy.com/official-tubidy-sites

## Core functions
- Search songs, artists and music videos with the search box on any page
- Download as MP3 (audio) or MP4 (video) from a song page
- [Browse by genre and mood](https://audio.tubidy.com/genre), e.g. [Amapiano](https://audio.tubidy.com/genre/amapiano)

## Guides
- [What is Tubidy? How the site works](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/what-is-tubidy): What Tubidy is, how searching and saving songs works, how MP3 and MP4 differ, and what the site is not: no account, no payment and no stored files.
- [Is Tubidy safe and legal to use?](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/is-tubidy-safe-and-legal): Safe habits for using Tubidy, how the law applies to downloading music, and how to report a problem or check that you are on the real Tubidy.
- [Tubidy not working? Fixes that actually help](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/tubidy-not-working): What to do when a Tubidy download does not start, stops halfway, the file will not play, storage is full or the site will not load at all.
- [How to download MP3 and MP4 on Android and iPhone](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/download-mp3-mp4-android-iphone): Step-by-step instructions for saving MP3 and MP4 files from Tubidy on Android with Chrome and on iPhone with Safari, plus where the files go.
- [Tubidy MP3 vs MP4: quality, file size and data](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/tubidy-mp3-vs-mp4): How MP3 audio and MP4 video differ on Tubidy, roughly how much data each uses, and which to choose on mobile data in South Africa and Ghana.
- [A commute playlist that survives a dead signal](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/commute-playlist-dead-signal): How to build a commute playlist that plays through tunnels and dead zones: how many songs to save, how to order them and how to test it before you go.
- [Fix missing cover art and tags](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/missing-cover-art-and-tags): Why a downloaded track can show no cover or the wrong name, how to check the file first, and how to fix its tags on a computer or a phone.
- [Listening offline: a short guide for travellers](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/listening-offline-travellers): How to pack music for a trip, how much to save, why MP3 suits flights, how to keep it in one folder and how to check it plays before you leave.
- [What bitrate actually changes about an MP3](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/what-bitrate-changes): What bitrate means for an MP3, how it sets file size and data use, where you will hear the difference, and a sensible default for phone listening.
- [Where downloads go on Android and iPhone](https://audio.tubidy.com/articles/where-downloads-go): Where to find a song after you tap download on Android and iPhone, how to tell the download finished, and how to get the file into your music app.

Every guide is also available in Spanish, French, Indonesian, Portuguese and Turkish at /<lang>/articles/<slug>, e.g. https://audio.tubidy.com/es/articles/what-is-tubidy.

